# Object translation delta (column D EN + new-field only)

English for object/field labels is **column D**, header `Field Label (EN)` (layout used on the 20 objects filled 2026-09-17), on the live Data Dictionary sheet
https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1_TaxDe-Qxl8BAUmuZc01vUoxpBEPxJ4Opx4tEe8ulNQ
Japanese `Field Label` (col C) remains `CustomField.label`. Locate the EN column by **header name**; only treat physical column D as EN when that header is present.

## Future field add (Japan team)

When a field is added to an object that already has translations:

1. Sheet row: JA in `Field Label`, EN in `Field Label (EN)` / col D, API in `fullName`. Honor WIP / IsDelete / `END[項目]` like every other field row.
2. `prep_deploy.py` Step 4b runs `translation_drift.py --new-only` against live `CustomObjectTranslation`.
3. Package **only** `NEW_TRANSLATION` (EN filled, no `en_US` translation in the org). `CHANGED_EN` is reported, not auto-packaged.
4. `generate_object_translation.py` **retrieves the org COT and merges the new field** so sibling translations are not wiped. The member `CustomObjectTranslation:<Obj>__c-en_US` rides in the **same** package as the new CustomField.

Do not invent English for a blank col D (WARN `MISSING_TRANSLATION`). Do not write col D into `generate_xml.py` field `<label>`.
